Package: castSDM
Type: Package
Title: Stable and Transferable Species Distribution Modeling
Version: 0.6.0
Author: Liqiang Q [aut, cre, cph] (ORCID: <https://orcid.org/0009-0002-6966-4633>)
Maintainer: Liqiang Q <2759831686@qq.com>
Authors@R: c(
    person(
            "Liqiang", "Q",
      email = "2759831686@qq.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
      comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0002-6966-4633")
    )
  )
Description: Provides an end-to-end species distribution modeling workflow
    built around a causal variable-selection engine. Double machine learning
    (Chernozhukov et al. 2018) estimates each predictor's orthogonalized
    partial-linear effect on occurrence while flexibly controlling for the
    others, and predictors surviving Benjamini-Hochberg FDR control are
    retained. The package couples this screen with standard SDM algorithms
    (Random Forest, BRT, MaxEnt, GAM), nested spatial cross-validation,
    ensemble prediction, future climate projection, and a counterfactual
    what-if interpretation layer. It supports transferable prediction and
    interpretable driver analysis but does not claim automatic discovery of
    ecological causes.
